    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d376">

                <pb facs="0542" n="436" xml:id="pg436"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Koppel to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1906-08-20"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">20 August, 1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith
                    printed copy of a circular dated 11 August, 1906, informing the governors of the
                    departments about a resolution passed by the council of ministers with regard to
                    a printed letter signed by the Colombian ex-minister at Washington, Señor Diego
                    Mendoza Perez, published in New York and bearing date of 2 July, 1906.</p>
                <p>According to this resolution, Señor Mendoza Perez has been declared traitor to
                    his country; and by Resolution 64 of 17 August, 1906, copy of which I also
                    inclose, he has been summoned to appear before the Colombian Government in this
                    city to answer the charges that have caused him to be declared traitor to the
                    country, otherwise his extradition is to be requested.</p>
                <p>Owing to pressure of time I am unable to send a translation of these articles,
                    and I will not delay them, as they may be of importance to the Department of
                    State.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sam B. Koppel</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">In charge.</hi></signed></closer>



